# fastly_ngwaf_workspace_rate_limit_rule (Resource)

Manages a Fastly Next-Gen WAF `rate_limit` rule scoped to a single workspace:
it counts matching requests per client and acts once they cross a threshold.

The `rate_limit` block is required and sets the threshold, the window, and
the custom signal used to count requests. `client_identifiers` decides how
requests are grouped into clients.

Rules of other types are managed by their own resources -
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_request_rule`,
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_signal_rule`, and
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_templated_signal_rule`. All four can be read back
together via the `fastly_ngwaf_workspace_rules` data source.

Every rule must define at least one `condition`, `group_condition`, or
`multival_condition`, and no more than 10 of them combined - a
`group_condition` or `multival_condition` counts as one entry however many
conditions it nests.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "fastly_ngwaf_workspace" "example" {
  name        = "Example Workspace"
  description = "Managed by Terraform"
  mode        = "block"

  attack_signal_thresholds {}
}

resource "fastly_ngwaf_workspace_rate_limit_rule" "rate_limit_example" {
  workspace_id = fastly_ngwaf_workspace.example.id
  description  = "Rate limit login attempts by IP"
  enabled      = true

  condition {
    field    = "path"
    operator = "equals"
    value    = "/login"
  }

  rate_limit {
    duration  = 300
    interval  = 60
    signal    = "site.excessive-login-attempts"
    threshold = 100

    client_identifiers {
      type = "ip"
    }

    client_identifiers {
      type = "request_cookie"
      name = "session_id"
    }
  }

  action {
    type   = "log_request"
    signal = "site.excessive-login-attempts"
  }
}
```

## Combining client identifiers

Only `ip` may be paired with a second `client_identifiers` entry; every other
type must be the sole entry.

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Import

Next-Gen WAF workspace rate limit rules are imported using a combination of
the workspace ID and the rule ID, separated by a `/`:

```shell
terraform import fastly_ngwaf_workspace_rate_limit_rule.example WORKSPACE_ID/RULE_ID
```
